Subject: [PATCH 1/4] fix(delta): replace dead `homework` collection with real
 `hw_assignments` (schema gap 1)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

DELTA_HARDENING.md §6 gap 1: the pull/delta allowlists carried the
collection name `homework`, but the migration chain, authz model,
SCHEMA_TABLES and the client (src/js/51-homework.js → db.hw_assignments)
all model homework as `hw_assignments`. Consequences before this fix:

- PG-live pull: readCollection('homework') → SELECT * FROM "homework"
  → 42P01 → the whole /api/v1/pull request 500s (latent, no PG-live
  default-pull test existed).
- Homework data never synced down: the response key `homework` merged
  into a client collection that does not exist; the real collection
  `hw_assignments` (table + migration 005-adjacent schema, updated_at
  present) was never served.

Fix: swap `homework` → `hw_assignments` in the canonical surface and
every mirror:

- server/pull.js ALL_COLLECTIONS (default pull + ?collections= filter)
- server/syncdelta.js ALLOWED (delta SQL builder allowlist)
- tests/wave4-sync-all-collections.js ALL fixture list
- tests/wave10-query-audit.js PULL_TABLES
- tools/delta-load-test.js ALL_COLLECTIONS

Old clients explicitly requesting ?collections=homework get it
silently dropped by the fail-closed collection filter (store has no
such collection either) — no crash, consistent with AC6 semantics.

Tests: tests/delta-schema-gaps.js (new) — SG1..SG5: builder accepts
hw_assignments and emits FROM "hw_assignments"; dead name rejected
fail-closed by syncdelta; default memory-mode pull serves
collections.hw_assignments (delta row only, school-scoped) and omits
homework; PG-live regression — no delta query is issued for the
missing table, pull stays 200; legacy ?collections=homework,grades
drops the dead name and serves grades. Phase-2 suites re-run green:
delta-sync-hardening 19/19, wave4-all-collections 13/13,
wave10-query-audit 14/14, contract-layers 18/18.
