Subject: [PATCH 2/4] fix(delta): drop dead `vclass_rooms`, serve real
 `vclass_sessions` (schema gap 2)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

DELTA_HARDENING.md §6 gap 2: `vclass_rooms` sat in the pull/delta
allowlists but has NO equivalent anywhere — no table in the migration
chain, not in SCHEMA_TABLES, not in the authz model, not in the client
store (the virtual-classroom domain is modeled as vclass_sessions /
vclass_questions / vclass_links / vclass_attendance).

Technical decision (per brief: «حذف از allowlist یا ساخت جدول؟ تصمیم
فنی بگیر»): REMOVE the dead name; do NOT create a table for a
collection with zero consumers. Creating a vclass_rooms table would be
schema noise nothing reads or writes. The real vclass pull surface is
vclass_sessions — school-scoped (school_id column ⇒ default
filterCollectionForSession scope rule), table + updated_at present —
which replaces it in the default list.

Deliberately NOT added to the default pull surface:
vclass_questions / vclass_links / vclass_attendance — their tables
carry only session_id/student_id and NO school_id, so the default
school-scope filter would treat every row as global and leak rows
across schools. Pulling them safely needs session→school scoping
machinery; documented as the known boundary in DELTA_HARDENING §6.

Changes (same surface + mirrors as gap 1):
- server/pull.js ALL_COLLECTIONS: vclass_rooms → vclass_sessions
- server/syncdelta.js ALLOWED: same
- tests/wave4-sync-all-collections.js: ALL list + AC10 fallback probe
  table switched to vclass_sessions
- tests/wave10-query-audit.js PULL_TABLES
- tools/delta-load-test.js ALL_COLLECTIONS

Legacy clients requesting ?collections=vclass_rooms get the name
silently dropped (fail-closed), consistent with gap-1 semantics.

Tests: tests/delta-schema-gaps.js SG6..SG8 — builder accepts
vclass_sessions (FROM "vclass_sessions") and rejects vclass_rooms
fail-closed; default pull serves collections.vclass_sessions and omits
vclass_rooms; school isolation: school-1 session never sees school-2
vclass rows and vice versa. SG4 extended to prove no delta query is
issued for either dead name in PG-live mode. Re-run green: wave4-all
13/13, wave10-query-audit 14/14, delta-sync-hardening 19/19,
contract-layers 18/18, delta-load-test DRY_RUN exit 0.
