DELTA_HARDENING.md §6 gap 3: sync_conflicts had created_at but NO
updated_at, while the delta pull predicate is
(created_at > $since OR updated_at > $since) ORDER BY updated_at, id —
in PG-live mode every sync_conflicts delta query died on the missing
column and the collection could never be delta-bounded.

migration 006_delta_schema_gaps.sql (+ .down), following the repo
conventions (idempotent guards, BEGIN/COMMIT, paired rollback, header
WHY — same no-CONCURRENTLY policy as 004/005):
- ALTER TABLE sync_conflicts ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS updated_at
  TIMESTAMPTZ
- UPDATE sync_conflicts SET updated_at = created_at
  WHERE updated_at IS NULL  (idempotent backfill per the brief's SQL)
- ALTER COLUMN updated_at SET NOT NULL
- CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_sync_conflicts_updated_at
- CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_hw_assignments_updated_at and
  idx_vclass_sessions_updated_at — the two collections that joined the
  delta surface in gaps 1-2 (same 005 policy: btree on updated_at for
  the OR predicate / ORDER BY).

Writers: no code path INSERTs into sync_conflicts today (Wave 1 keeps
arbitration state cache-side — see the apiResolve note), so SET NOT
NULL breaks nothing; the stamps below make the future mirror path
correct from day one:
- server/sync.js: new conflict rows carry updated_at: nowIso
  (=== created_at).
- server/conflicts.js apiResolve: resolving stamps
  c.updated_at = c.resolved_at. Without it a long-lived conflict that
  gets adjudicated NOW would never surface in any client's delta pull
  (created_at stays old) — the exact hole the column closes.

Tests (tests/delta-schema-gaps.js SG9..SG12, now 12/12): 006 file
contract (idempotent column add, backfill, NOT NULL, all three
indexes, transactional up + down that drops them); conflict row from
the real two-op sync path carries updated_at === created_at; resolve
stamps updated_at === resolved_at (fresh); delta of a store whose old
conflict was resolved recently returns exactly that row via
updated_at. Re-run green: delta-sync-hardening 19/19 (incl. DH15/16
conflict witnesses), contract-layers 18/18, wave4-all 13/13,
wave10-query-audit 14/14.
